LICENSE
=======

This repository is a modified copy of the FreeBASIC compiler (fbc), so it
carries FreeBASIC's licensing unchanged. Nothing here is relicensed, and no
licence was chosen for this work -- it is inherited.

FreeBASIC is licensed in two parts, and the USTRING work touches both, so both
apply:


1. THE COMPILER  --  GNU GPL, version 2 or later
------------------------------------------------

Everything under src/compiler/, and the fbc32.exe / fbc64.exe / bin/fbc
binaries built from it (including those shipped in fbc-win/ and fbc-linux/).

Full text: COPYING.GPL-2.0


2. THE RUNTIME AND GRAPHICS LIBRARIES  --  GNU LGPL, version 2.1 or later,
   with a static-linking exception
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under src/rtlib/ and src/gfxlib2/ -- that is libfb, libfbmt,
libfbgfx and libfbgfxmt, including the libraries shipped in fbc-win/lib/ and
fbc-linux/lib/.

Full text: COPYING.LGPL-2.1

The exception, quoted from FreeBASIC's own readme.txt, is what allows a program
to link the runtime statically without taking on the LGPL:

    As a special exception, the copyright holders of this library give
    you permission to link this library with independent modules to
    produce an executable, regardless of the license terms of these
    independent modules, and to copy and distribute the resulting
    executable under terms of your choice, provided that you also meet,
    for each linked independent module, the terms and conditions of the
    license of that module. An independent module is a module which is
    not derived from or based on this library. If you modify this library,
    you may extend this exception to your version of the library, but
    you are not obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete
    this exception statement from your version.


3. DOCUMENTATION  --  GNU FDL
------------------------------

FreeBASIC's documentation, including fbc-master/doc/. The USTRING user
documentation, fbc-master/doc/ustring.txt, is part of that.


WHICH LICENCE APPLIES TO THE USTRING WORK
-----------------------------------------

It follows the file, exactly as it does for the rest of fbc:

  src/compiler/*                 GPLv2+       keyword, datatype, backends,
                                              rtl-ustring.bas
  src/rtlib/ustr_*.c             LGPLv2.1+    the runtime: descriptors,
  src/rtlib/fb_ustring.h         with the     codecs, intrinsics, I/O
  src/rtlib/ustr_wchar_conv.h    exception
  src/gfxlib2/gfx_drawstring_ustr.c
  src/gfxlib2/gfx_cp437.h

  doc/ustring.txt                GNU FDL

  tests/, tools/, NOTES.md, README.md
                                 GPLv2+, same as the compiler they test and
                                 describe


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS SHIPPED IN THE PREBUILT TREES
----------------------------------------------------

fbc-win/ and fbc-linux/ contain more than FreeBASIC. They redistribute the
toolchain and support libraries fbc invokes and links against, each under its
own licence:

  fbc-win/bin/win32, fbc-win/bin/win64
      GNU binutils (as, ld, ar, ...) and gcc -- GPLv3
  fbc-win/lib/win32, fbc-win/lib/win64
      MinGW-w64 runtime and import libraries, plus libgcc and libstdc++,
      under their own terms (MinGW-w64 is largely public-domain / BSD-style;
      libgcc and libstdc++ carry the GCC Runtime Library Exception)

These are unmodified redistributions. See the licence files in those
directories, and the "Dependencies on third-party libraries" section of
fbc-master/readme.txt.

LibFFI, used by the runtime for ThreadCall, is under the MIT/Expat licence --
see fbc-master/doc/libffi-license.txt. Note that the Windows binaries here were
built with -DDISABLE_FFI and do not link it; the Linux build does.


